  "name": "G6PD DEFICIENCY (QUALITATIVE)",
  "code": "1557",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"101\" data-end=\"167\">G6PD is an <strong data-start=\"112\" data-end=\"122\">enzyme</strong> essential for red blood cell (RBC) function.</p>\n<p data-start=\"170\" data-end=\"260\">It protects RBCs from oxidative damage by maintaining <strong data-start=\"224\" data-end=\"239\">glutathione</strong> in its reduced form.</p>\n<p data-start=\"263\" data-end=\"406\">Deficiency can lead to <strong data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"299\">hemolysis</strong> (destruction of RBCs), especially under stress (like infections, certain drugs, or foods like fava beans).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>G6PD Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong></td>\n<td>Adequate enzyme activity. Unlikely to have G6PD deficiency.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mildly Reduced</strong></td>\n<td>Possible <strong>partial deficiency</strong>. May show symptoms only under significant stress.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low or Absent</strong></td>\n<td><strong>G6PD Deficiency</strong>. High risk for <strong>hemolytic anemia</strong>, especially under triggers.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1340\" data-end=\"1370\"><strong data-start=\"1344\" data-end=\"1370\">Clinical Significance:</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1396\"><strong data-start=\"1377\" data-end=\"1396\">G6PD Deficiency</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1397\" data-end=\"1614\">\n<li data-start=\"1397\" data-end=\"1451\">\n<p data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1451\"><strong data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1428\">X-linked genetic disorder</strong>, more common in males.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1452\" data-end=\"1614\">\n<p data-start=\"1454\" data-end=\"1509\">Can lead to <strong data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1492\">acute hemolytic anemia</strong> when exposed to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1614\">\n<li data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1584\">\n<p data-start=\"1514\" data-end=\"1584\">Certain medications (e.g., sulfa drugs, antimalarials, nitrofurantoin)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1587\" data-end=\"1599\">\n<p data-start=\"1589\" data-end=\"1599\">Infections</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1602\" data-end=\"1614\">\n<p data-start=\"1604\" data-end=\"1614\">Fava beans</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1616\" data-end=\"1666\"><strong data-start=\"1621\" data-end=\"1666\">Symptoms of Hemolysis in G6PD Deficiency:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1667\" data-end=\"1746\">\n<li data-start=\"1667\" data-end=\"1683\">\n<p data-start=\"1669\" data-end=\"1683\">Sudden fatigue</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1684\" data-end=\"1694\">\n<p data-start=\"1686\" data-end=\"1694\">Jaundice</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1695\" data-end=\"1715\">\n<p data-start=\"1697\" data-end=\"1715\">Dark-colored urine</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1716\" data-end=\"1734\">\n<p data-start=\"1718\" data-end=\"1734\">Rapid heart rate</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1735\" data-end=\"1746\">\n<p data-start=\"1737\" data-end=\"1746\">Back pain</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
